    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0658" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2864: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-24T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24, 1920—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>190. Your No. 180, July 11, noon.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d546-f1"/> Department
                    does not believe it advisable that applications of Chinese Government for loans
                    under the Consortium should be made to the Legation. More orderly method would
                    be for Chinese Government to apply to the four Group representatives in
                    Peking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
